      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "BL Or. 6197.7r (ninth section in join)",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>\n<p>When the word had spread, [the ki]ng summoned Yehudah</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>he gardener and said to him: &ldquo;The man whom you (sg.) have crucified&mdash;what did you do with him?&rdquo;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>And he (i.e., Yehudah) said: &ldquo;I buried him in the garden.&rdquo; And the king said to him: &ldquo;What is this calumny</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>that is hea[rd?&rdquo; And he said] to him: &ldquo;Oh king, the cursed Yeshu knew</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>[that it is wr]itten in the Torah that one who is crucified&mdash;&lsquo;Do not let his corpse remain overnight on</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>the tree&rsquo;, and he deceived his followers and said to them: &lsquo;If you come tomorrow and do not</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>find me on the cross, know that I ascended to [Heav]en&rsquo;.&rdquo; And the king said</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>to Yehudah the gardener: &ldquo;Dig him out and bring him.&rdquo;&nbsp;Yehudah the gardener dug him out and fastened</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>a rope to his leg and dragged him through the markets of Tiberias. And it was proclaimed about him: &ldquo;This is Yeshu</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>the heretic who violated God&rsquo;s will&mdash;recognise him!&rdquo; Some of his followers</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>believed it (i.e., that it is the body of Yeshu) and some of them did not believe.&nbsp;Then the king said to Yehudah:</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>&ldquo;[Just] as you saw fit when&nbsp;burying him in the garden,&nbsp;bury him with the [rest of?]</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>the dead.&rdquo; And he (i.e., Yehudah) did so. The day of Yeshu was the fourteenth of Nisan, and the day Yeshu was dug out</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>dragged through the markets of Tiberias was the twenty-second of Nisan. He who took revenge upon Yeshu&mdash;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>He will take revenge upon the heretics and the worshipers of idols. King Tiberinus</p>\n</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
